+    HostTraceVariant::allocate makes them before the run's graph is queued. In "eager" order (a run with
+    an order): its temporaries (made at their seq, freed after their last use), its tensors (never freed
+    in the run), its freed arguments, and a section's own temporaries (made before the op's first launch,
+    freed after its last). A run buffer's run (temporaries, no order): its temporaries, placed first fit
+    over their lifetimes; a section's are held over the run. A run of tensors only: its tensors, and a
+    section's own temporaries, made and freed before the first tensor the op's chain makes. A base absent
+    holds its bytes over the run (made before it, held or relocated, an eager output, a dropped one)."""
